From: Dana Fried <dfried@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:27:18 -0800
Subject: [Views] Spot-protect button updates in dialogs.

This prevents a case where badly-configured or malicious accessibility
handlers modify a dialog in the middle of the dialog buttons being
modified.

Fixed: 583617538
Change-Id: I97caee769d7cdf09ddaa031b8c409b9a3f414ed6
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8772989
Reviewed-by: Caroline Rising <corising@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Dana Fried <dfried@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Dana Fried <dfried@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1739349}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
ViewGuard comes from the picked prerequisite d9fcba36b9c9
(https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8652648).

diff --git a/ui/views/window/dialog_client_view.cc b/ui/views/window/dialog_client_view.cc
index 9252a91ce3c1510ea36e6cebd3d2fadf74a5ed56..9c6b4e9f23011ce974959c811548967a83ce1100 100644
--- a/ui/views/window/dialog_client_view.cc
+++ b/ui/views/window/dialog_client_view.cc
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
 #include "ui/views/metadata/view_factory.h"
 #include "ui/views/style/platform_style.h"
 #include "ui/views/view_class_properties.h"
+#include "ui/views/view_guard.h"
 #include "ui/views/view_observer.h"
 #include "ui/views/view_tracker.h"
 #include "ui/views/view_utils.h"
@@ -376,6 +377,15 @@ void DialogClientView::UpdateDialogButton(raw_ptr<MdTextButton>* member,
   const ui::ButtonStyle style = delegate->GetDialogButtonStyle(type);
 
   if (*member) {
+    // Accessibility events sent while updating buttons could theoretically
+    // result in synchronous destruction of the dialog or re-entrancy into this
+    // method via malicious or badly-configured software that hooks
+    // accessibility callbacks.
+    //
+    // Since these errors are difficult to fully protect against, guard the
+    // dialog during these updates instead.
+    ViewGuard guard(*member->get());
+
     MdTextButton* button = *member;
     button->SetEnabled(delegate->IsDialogButtonEnabled(type));
     button->SetIsDefault(is_default);
